Also allows people to shoot at the shopkeepers more easily, which is
one of the reasons they don't come to the door in the first place.

As best I can tell, the intent ("feel free to correct me, anonymous
watchers") was that players should only be easily able to use ranged weaponry
against shopkeepers from inside the shopkeeper's store -- in other
words, without an easy place to run if the combat failed, and so that
the shopkeeper isn't trapped unable to leave his shop and thus leave it
open for a "very fast" player to dodge around and steal, beartrap the
shopkeeper, etc.  I don't want to disturb this without some better reasons.

